# interplay_displaywalk_38: Seeded random walks over display state (pgtest/randdisplay.py): each seed is one scenario, interplay_displaywalk_<seed>, whose program the generator builds from the seed alone.  A walk drives one or two display ports and the EFI framebuffer through random legal guest and host actions: connects on fresh and reused pages, acks, disconnects, hot plugs and unplugs, mode lists (the same one, new ones, 130 modes), presents of task 0's backings (opcodes 6, 7) and of mapper surfaces (8) with gamma tables of 2 to 1024 entries, colour matrices, ICC profiles, protection options, sleep and wake, cursor glyphs from 1 x 1 to 256 x 256, shows, moves and the doorbell, refused presents and commands the version gates, the guest rewriting backings and surfaces under the frames, backings deleted and surfaces unmapped and mapped again; pause and unpause with host changes and guest commands rung while paused, suspend onto a fresh device and resume, reset and stop with the guest's set-up again, and EFI at boot and after a reset. Some programs end in a death docs/testing.md lists (7.3, 7.4).  A model restated from the guest display's and the display's code predicts every observation: the callbacks and interrupts, every shared page byte for byte (compared with a mirror of the model's bytes), 0x1014 and 0x1018, the root page's display words, the encoded pixels, present counts and cursor positions (pgtest.randdisplay.check reads the expected files back; python3 -m pgtest.randdisplay). Programs with mapper surfaces run in map and isolate, the others in all three setups. The encoded frames make every program host-keyed.  This program: 2 ports, version 245, mapper surfaces; ack 6, bogus_state 1, clear_raised 1, compositor 1, connect 5, delete_backing 2, efi 2, encode 2, glyph 4, icc 3, matrix 2, move 2, pause 2, plug 1, present6 1, present_backing 3, present_mapped 11, reconnect 1, remap_surface 1, reset 2, rewrite_backing 1, rewrite_surface 3, ring_while_paused 2, scribble 2, set_modes 3, show 1, suspend 1, unpause 2, unplug 2; ends in a death (cursor_paused).
